## Ⅰ. WFL — WORK FLOW LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   WFL
FULL NAME:      Work Flow Language
LATIN:          Lingua Fluxus Operis
ROLE:           How you actually work — bursts, sprints, deep dives, wandering
FREQUENCY:      396 Hz (liberation — freedom in how you work)
GLYPH:          𓌙 (flowing water — the current of work)
```

### What WFL Governs
```
THE SHAPE OF WORK ITSELF:
    ├── Bursts — intense short periods
    ├── Sprints — focused multi-day efforts
    ├── Deep dives — extended immersion in one domain
    ├── Wandering — exploratory unfocused time
    ├── Energy cycles — when energy is high/low
    ├── Context switching — cost and management of switching domains
    └── Recovery — how rest and restoration happen between work

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    ORGANISM_SPACE/CANISTERS/W_OPERATIONS.canister (operations workflow)
    src/organism/Heart.mo (873ms heartbeat — the rhythm of work)
    ARCHITECTURE_DOCTRINE.md (oxygen connection: inhale→process→exhale→integrate)
    CODEX_VIVENS.md §VI (PIL 52-beat cycle: learn→understand→execute→adapt→teach)
```

### WFL Primitives
```
BURST(duration, intensity, domain)   — intense short work
SPRINT(days, goal, scope)            — multi-day focused effort
DEEP_DIVE(domain, duration)          — extended immersion
WANDER(direction_hint)               — exploratory time
ENERGY(level, forecast)              — current energy state
SWITCH(from_context, to_context)     — context switch with cost
RECOVER(method, duration)            — scheduled recovery
RHYTHM(pattern, cycle_length)        — repeating work pattern
INTERRUPT(priority, handler)         — how interruptions are handled
```

---

## Ⅱ. CXL — CREATION LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   CXL
FULL NAME:      Creation Language
LATIN:          Lingua Creationis
ROLE:           How new things emerge from nothing
FREQUENCY:      528 Hz (transformation — creation is transformation of nothing into something)
GLYPH:          𓆣 (scarab — the self-creating being)
```

### What CXL Governs
```
THE GENESIS PIPELINE:
    ├── Idea — the first spark, before form
    ├── Sketch — rough shape, exploring possibility
    ├── Prototype — first functional form
    ├── Organism — living, self-sustaining creation
    ├── Civilization — creation that creates further
    └── The void — what exists before the idea (links to PIL)

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    ORGANISM_SPACE/GENESIS/GENESIS_CREATION_DOCUMENT.artifact
    ORGANISM_SPACE/GENESIS/AI_SEED_KERNEL.artifact
    DEPLOYMENT.organism §4 (Seed Compiler — minimal viable organism)
    packages/organism-kernel/ (OrganismState: DORMANT → AWAKENING → ALIVE)
```

### CXL Primitives
```
SPARK(idea, origin)                    — the first moment of creation
SKETCH(idea, rough_form)               — give idea rough shape
PROTOTYPE(sketch, functional_form)     — first working version
ORGANISM(prototype, self_sustaining)   — it lives on its own
CIVILIZATION(organisms[], governance)  — creation that creates
VOID(potential)                        — the space before creation
ITERATE(creation, feedback, version)   — refine creation
BIRTH(creation, into_world)            — deploy creation into a realm
LINEAGE(creation, parent, ancestry)    — provenance of creation
```

---

## Ⅲ. EXL — EXPERIMENT LANGUAGE

```
ABBREVIATION:   EXL
FULL NAME:      Experiment Language
LATIN:          Lingua Experimentorum
ROLE:           How you run experiments and accept risk
FREQUENCY:      417 Hz (transmutation — experiments change things)
GLYPH:          𓃀 (fire — testing by fire)
```

### What EXL Governs
```
THE SCIENCE OF TRYING:
    ├── Hypotheses — what you think will happen
    ├── Probes — small tests to gather information
    ├── Kill-switches — when to stop an experiment
    ├── Learnings — what was gained regardless of outcome
    ├── Risk acceptance — explicit statement of what could go wrong
    └── Experiment lifecycle — propose→test→observe→conclude→integrate

EXISTING PATTERNS:
    ORGANISM_SPACE/CANISTERS/W_ANALYST.canister (analysis + experiment)
    ORGANISM_SPACE/CANISTERS/W_RISK.canister (risk assessment)
    GOVERNANCE.organism §5 (ORACULUM prediction before action)
    SECURITY.organism §7 (post-incident analysis — experiment on failure)
```

### EXL Primitives
```
HYPOTHESIS(statement, expected_outcome)   — what you think will happen
PROBE(target, method, duration)           — small test
KILL_SWITCH(experiment, condition)         — stop condition
OBSERVE(experiment, metrics[])            — what to watch
CONCLUDE(experiment, outcome, vs_expected) — end and evaluate
LEARN(experiment, lessons[])              — extract lessons
RISK(experiment, what_could_go_wrong)     — explicit risk statement
INTEGRATE(learnings, into_system)         — feed back into organism
```

---

## Ⅳ. CREATION LIFECYCLE

```
VOID (CXL) → SPARK → SKETCH → HYPOTHESIS (EXL) → PROBE → OBSERVE
                         │                                    │
                         ▼                                    ▼
                    PROTOTYPE (CXL)                    CONCLUDE + LEARN
                         │                                    │
                         ▼                                    ▼
                    ORGANISM (CXL)                   INTEGRATE (EXL → WFL)
                         │
                         ▼
                    CIVILIZATION

    Work flow (WFL) is the rhythm WITHIN which creation (CXL) and
    experimentation (EXL) happen. WFL is the container.
    CXL is the genesis. EXL is the testing.
```

